== Match report ==

=== Sanrobonia 2–1 Orma ===
[[Sanrobonia national football team|Sanrobonia]] advanced to the final after a hard-fought victory over [[Orma national football team|Orma]] in [[Castejón]]. The match was goalless at half-time, with neither side able to find the breakthrough in a tightly contested first 45 minutes.

The deadlock was finally broken in the 53rd minute when [[Dante Palar]] scored for Sanrobonia. However, Orma's tournament top scorer [[Mikael Dirra]] equalised just four minutes later in the 57th minute, keeping Orma's remarkable comeback tradition alive. But Sanrobonia were not to be denied, and [[Gabriel Somba]] scored the winner in the 77th minute to send the co-hosts to their first AFA World Cup final.

Orma's extraordinary run of comebacks — having previously overturned deficits against the United Midlands and Varkana — finally ended in the semi-final.

=== Balisca 0–1 Asikyira ===
Co-hosts [[Balisca national football team|Balisca]] were knocked out of the tournament by [[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]] in [[Concepción]], with [[Amadou Baal]] scoring a dramatic late winner in the 93rd minute of stoppage time.

The match was tightly contested throughout, with both sides creating chances but unable to find the net. Balisca pushed hard in the second half, but Asikyira's defence held firm. Just as the match seemed headed for extra time, Baal — the tournament's leading scorer — struck in the dying moments to break Baliscan hearts and send Asikyira to the final.

== Summary ==

The semi-finals produced 4 goals across 2 matches. [[Sanrobonia national football team|Sanrobonia]] and [[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]] advanced to the final, while co-hosts [[Balisca national football team|Balisca]] were eliminated on home soil.

The tournament's final will be contested between co-hosts Sanrobonia and Asikyira on 10 July at the [[Campo Simpliciano]] in [[Castejón]]. The third-place match will see Balisca face Orma on 9 July at the [[Stadion Agung Martapura]] in [[Martapura]].

